      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(0.3),$ compute $P(X=1).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}p, & x=1 \\\\ 1-p, & x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(0.3),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.3, & x=1 \\\\ 0.7, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=1)=f(1)=0.3.\n$$",
